==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|motor|ize}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To fit something with a [[motor]].
#: {{ux|en|Most canoe aficionados would argue that '''motorizing''' a canoe removes the pleasurable aspects of traveling in one.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To supply something or someone with [[motor vehicle]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Once Jack decided to '''motorize''' his paper delivery route, he found he could reach far more subscribers.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To supply [[armour]]ed vehicles; to [[mechanize]].
#: {{ux|en|The refit plan recommended that the first battalion be '''motorized''' to upgrade their offensive capabilities.}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|motorise}}

